              "id": "CVE-2026-54290",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "hono: CORS Middleware reflects any Origin with credentials when `origin` defaults to the wildcard"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Hono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. Prior to 4.12.25, with credentials: true and no explicit origin (the default wildcard), the CORS Middleware reflects the request's Origin and sends Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true. Any site can then make credentialed cross-origin requests and read the responses, exposing cookie-authenticated endpoints to arbitrary origins. This vulnerability is fixed in 4.12.25."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54290",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54290\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: hono\nFixed Version: 4.12.25\nLink: [CVE-2026-54290](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54290)\nHono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. Prior to 4.12.25, with credentials: true and no explicit origin (the default wildcard), the CORS Middleware reflects the request's Origin and sends Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true. Any site can then make credentialed cross-origin requests and read the responses, exposing cookie-authenticated endpoints to arbitrary origins. This vulnerability is fixed in 4.12.25.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-54290**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|hono|4.12.25|[CVE-2026-54290](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54290)|\n\nHono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. Prior to 4.12.25, with credentials: true and no explicit origin (the default wildcard), the CORS Middleware reflects the request's Origin and sends Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true. Any site can then make credentialed cross-origin requests and read the responses, exposing cookie-authenticated endpoints to arbitrary origins. This vulnerability is fixed in 4.12.25."
              },
